INT. AUCTION HOUSE - CLOAKROOM - NIGHT

Rows of coat hooks, a long counter, brass tickets in a bowl. Muffled applause through the wall. A marble clock ticks.

BARONESS ISADORA KELLERMAN-OYE (60s, fur stole, emerald choker) stands at the counter. HUGO LINDENBAUM (30s, tuxedo, cloakroom attendant's bow tie slightly crooked) holds up a coat. INSPECTOR FELICITY ANGWIN (40s, dark overcoat) leans against the far wall, notebook open.

ISADORA
Hugo, I gave you the ticket at nine.

HUGO
Baroness, you gave me a ticket at nine. I assumed it was for the stole.

ISADORA
The stole is on my shoulders.

FELICITY
Baroness, may I ask what was in the coat?

ISADORA
A letter.

HUGO
A letter, ma'am?

FELICITY
Hugo, let her answer.

ISADORA
A letter from my late husband, to be read aloud this evening at the sale, which is why I was so careful about the ticket.

HUGO
(overlapping)
I gave it back to a gentleman.

FELICITY
(overlapping)
Which gentleman?

ISADORA
(overlapping)
What gentleman?

HUGO
Tall. Beard. Blue ribbon in his lapel.

ISADORA
That is the auctioneer!

FELICITY
He's been on the dais all night.

HUGO
Then it was someone dressed as him.

ISADORA
Hugo, you gave my husband's last words to an impostor!

HUGO
Ma'am, in my defence, he was very convincing.

FELICITY
Baroness, was the letter in an envelope?

ISADORA
Cream. Sealed with green wax. My initials in the corner.

FELICITY
And what did the letter say?

ISADORA
That is none of your concern.

FELICITY
It may be of great concern. A man was found in the carriage house this evening. In his pocket, a cream envelope.

ISADORA
(sharp breath)
Dead?

FELICITY
Yes.

A long silence. Applause through the wall again, rising, then falling away. Hugo puts down the coat.

HUGO
Ma'am. I swear I didn't know.

ISADORA
(low)
Of course you didn't.

FELICITY
Baroness, do you know the man?

ISADORA
No. I never saw him before in my life.

FELICITY
Then why are you crying?

ISADORA
Because he has my husband's face.

Felicity closes the notebook. Hugo picks up the tuxedo coat and holds it out like a shield.
